					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-474114#post-1472601</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-474114/lord-blackwood-in-the-land-of-the-unclean#post-1472601</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 06 Jun 2012 16:05:43 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Adam Henderson</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1350867</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I love Blackwood. He is a great new way of describing SCP items.</p> <p>Also, what do you think of any of these ideas for further adventures of His Lordship?</p> <p><strong>1. Lord Blackwood and the Changelings:</strong> In a small town, in Britain's American colonies children are vanishing. Strange, red-skinned and eyeless beasts with the power to mimic voices run wild. It is into this nightmare of a town which Lord Blackwood arrives with the twin goals of solving the riddle of the missing children, and bagging a monster <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-939">with many voices</a>.</p> <p><strong>2. Lord Blackwood at Sea:</strong> A voyage to capture a <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-879">whale-like monster</a> preying upon shipping. Throw in pirates, storms, other adventures joining the hunt and this may be more of a threat to His Lordship than it seems&#8230;.</p> <p><strong>3. Lord Blackwood and the Sky-Discs:</strong> His Lordship takes to the skies in an airship on the hunt for a flock of <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-994">strange flying animals</a>, unlike anything ever seen before.</p> <p><strong>4. Lord Blackwood on the Dark Continent:</strong> A thrilling expedition 'cross Darkest Africa for the rarest of beasts, the <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-131">eye-pods</a>.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
